  "summary_en": "Bahrain's 2017 Cloud First Policy, issued by the Information and eGovernment Authority, directs government entities to evaluate cloud services in ICT procurement to cut costs, improve security and productivity. It covers cloud models, security principles, data classification, data sovereignty, and roles of iGA, ICTGC and SCICT. It does not address AI or robotics.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "All government agencies must evaluate cloud-based services in ICT procurements.",
   "Adopts NIST cloud computing definition and service/deployment models.",
   "Sets cloud security, data classification, backup and data sovereignty requirements.",
   "iGA acts as interface with cloud providers and monitors SLAs.",
   "ICTGC oversees implementation and audits entity compliance."
  ],
